{
  "name": "22-mirror-coverage-order-master-first",
  "why": "Stage 4.5 ordering, the other way round: master and cover are evaluated BEFORE the client. On the web they stop out their own t1 / leg1 at market (t1 at ask 1.10020 = -10020, leg1 at bid 1.10000 = -10020, NBP floors both at 0) with STOP_OUT / COVERAGE_STOP_OUT notices, and leg1's close RELEASES the still-open client p1 with a COVERAGE_STOP_OUT notice to the desk. The client's later stop-out then finds t1 closed (mirror no-op) and p1 unhedged. The engine must reach the same end: nothing is pending when master and cover are evaluated, and the client waits until leg1's follow-up released p1.",
